            stem: "After the Supreme Court held that a federal statute of limitations barred a category of private fraud suits, many federal courts dismissed such suits, and the dismissals became final when no appeal was taken. Congress then enacted a statute directing federal courts to reinstate, on a plaintiff's motion made within sixty days, any suit that had been dismissed as time-barred under that decision. A plaintiff whose suit was dismissed by a final judgment moves for reinstatement under the new statute. The defendant argues that the statute is unconstitutional as applied.",
