            stem: "A state prison guard assaulted a prisoner in violation of the Eighth Amendment. The prisoner sued the guard in federal court under 42 U.S.C. §1983, naming the guard in his personal capacity only and seeking money damages to be paid by the guard. The State is not a party and has not consented to be sued. The guard moves to dismiss on the ground that the Eleventh Amendment bars the suit.",
