            say: "The President may remove executive officers at will; Congress cannot keep removal for itself, and for-cause shields for executive power are suspect.",
            elements: ["The President may remove executive officers at will (Myers)", "Congress may not reserve removal for itself or its own officers (Bowsher)", "A single agency head wielding executive power may not be shielded by for-cause protection (Seila Law)", "Two layers of for-cause protection are invalid (Free Enterprise Fund)"],
