            stem: "A federal statute authorizes the Attorney General to suspend the deportation of noncitizens who meet specified hardship criteria. The statute provides that either House of Congress may, by a simple resolution passed within a set period, veto any suspension. The Attorney General suspends a noncitizen's deportation; one House then passes a resolution vetoing the suspension, and the government orders the noncitizen deported. The noncitizen challenges the one-House veto.",
