            stem: "Congress enacts a statute requiring the chief law-enforcement officer of each county to conduct a background check on every applicant to buy a handgun, during the five years before a national federal system takes effect. The statute was enacted after a two-year national debate, and the sheriff's county has 80,000 residents and a small, understaffed sheriff's department. A county sheriff who is subject to the requirement sues the federal government, seeking a declaration that the requirement is invalid as applied to him.",
