            stem: "Congress enacts a statute with two provisions about sports gambling. The first makes it a federal crime for any private person to operate a sports lottery. The second makes it unlawful for any State to authorize, by law, sports gambling schemes within its borders. The United States sues a State whose legislature has legalized sports betting, to enforce the second provision. The State argues that the second provision violates the Tenth Amendment.",
