            stem: "Federal law makes it unlawful for an employer to hire a worker who is not authorized to work in the United States, and it imposes civil and criminal penalties on employers who do so. Congress considered and rejected criminal penalties for workers who seek or accept unauthorized work. A State then makes it a state misdemeanor for an unauthorized worker to apply for, solicit, or perform work in the State. The State prosecutes a worker, who defends on the ground that federal law preempts the state provision. The federal statute contains no express preemption clause aimed at state penalties on workers. The worker has lived in the State for six years.",
