            stem: "A State permits wineries located in the State to ship wine directly to consumers in the State, but requires out-of-state wineries to sell only through licensed in-state wholesalers, which add costs and keep out-of-state wineries from reaching many consumers. The State defends the law as a regulation of alcohol enacted under the Twenty-first Amendment, which gives States power over the transportation and importation of intoxicating liquors. Consumers and an out-of-state winery that has made wine for more than a century sue to invalidate the law under the Commerce Clause. Congress has not legislated on the subject.",
